  "query_preview": "../Monday through Wednesday...Little change to the \nlong term forecast and overall message as the pattern looks to \nstay unsettled. Low pressure will remain nearly stationary and \nvery slowly weaken over south-central Alaska through the period. \nThis will send multiple fronts across the panhandle and also work \nto reinforce persistent onshore flow. As a result, we will \ncontinue to see periods of rain, especially Monday into Tuesday \nwith perhaps a bit less widespread precipitation for a time later \nWednesday. As weak high pressure builds to our east over British \nColumbia and the pressure gradient tightens, we may see intervals \nof gusty winds, particularly in the favored areas over the \nnorthern panhandle. Model guidance is also suggesting that we \ncould see a few thunderstorms, mainly over the coastal waters, but\nconfidence was too low to include in the forecast at this time.",
